WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.802 --> 00:00:03.770
[music playing]

00:00:03.837 --> 00:00:04.804
MAN: We are here to
document the lives

00:00:04.871 --> 00:00:06.206
of people living in Alaska.

00:00:06.272 --> 00:00:08.274
The harsh reality is the
environment we're up against.

00:00:08.341 --> 00:00:09.542
It makes it tough to do our job.

00:00:09.609 --> 00:00:11.044
NATHANIEL "NATCHO"
STEPHENS: Get out of there.

00:00:11.111 --> 00:00:12.946
MAN: Working on "Life Below
Zero" can be very dangerous.

00:00:13.012 --> 00:00:14.080
MAN: Gun's here.

00:00:14.147 --> 00:00:15.882
Camera's here.
MAN: Never know what to expect.

00:00:15.949 --> 00:00:16.816
MAN: Whoa!

00:00:16.883 --> 00:00:18.051
Did you [bleep]
see that [bleep]??

00:00:18.118 --> 00:00:20.720
MAN: Gonna be tough, but
we're going to get the shot.

00:00:20.787 --> 00:00:22.655
MAN: Every scenario, we
gotta prepare for this.

00:00:22.722 --> 00:00:24.424
NATHANIEL "NATCHO" STEPHENS:
But we're still smiling.

00:00:24.491 --> 00:00:25.558
We're having fun.

00:00:25.625 --> 00:00:28.228
Still making "Life Below Zero."

00:00:28.294 --> 00:00:29.329
Yes.

00:00:29.396 --> 00:00:30.096
Bring it on.

00:00:43.009 --> 00:00:44.778
So of all the
things that we do

00:00:44.844 --> 00:00:47.180
working on "Life Below
Zero," I would say this

00:00:47.247 --> 00:00:49.516
is one of the most challenging.

00:00:49.582 --> 00:00:53.553
It's our travel day to the
Hailstones Kiwalik Camp.

00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:55.388
The biggest challenge
is getting out there.

00:00:55.455 --> 00:00:57.924
We can only get
to about 100 miles

00:00:57.991 --> 00:01:00.627
away from where
we're going by plane.

00:01:00.693 --> 00:01:04.497
And then the rest of the way,
we need to go on snow machines,

00:01:04.564 --> 00:01:06.966
hauling sleds with
some of our gear.

00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:10.203
We are right at the
edge of the peninsula.

00:01:10.270 --> 00:01:14.741
So we'll be traveling over
sea ice for the next 40 miles.

00:01:14.808 --> 00:01:17.911
The ice is very dynamic
out here on the ocean.

00:01:17.977 --> 00:01:20.146
It's breaking and
coming together.

00:01:20.213 --> 00:01:22.949
It's being moved by the
tides and by the winds.

00:01:23.016 --> 00:01:24.417
And it's a little bit dangerous.

00:01:24.484 --> 00:01:28.455
But we mitigate those
dangers by making a good plan

00:01:28.521 --> 00:01:33.393
and taking our time and being
thoughtful about how we travel.

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:34.194
All right, boys.

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:34.994
You ready for this?

00:01:35.061 --> 00:01:35.895
Let's do it!

00:01:35.962 --> 00:01:37.831
NATHANIEL "NATCHO"
STEPHENS: Yes.

00:01:37.897 --> 00:01:39.165
So we're right on target.

00:01:39.232 --> 00:01:41.100
We've got a couple
hours of daylight left.

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:43.837
And it looks like we should
be fine to get into camp

00:01:43.903 --> 00:01:47.173
and make some shelter
before it's totally dark.

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:48.975
It's incredible that
we get to do this,

00:01:49.042 --> 00:01:51.744
that this is our job, riding
across the Arctic Ocean.

00:01:51.811 --> 00:01:54.380
And we're really
feeling lucky right now.

00:02:04.657 --> 00:02:08.061
MAN: We arrived here just
before dark last night,

00:02:08.127 --> 00:02:09.462
after our 100 mile trip.

00:02:09.529 --> 00:02:11.397
NATHANIEL "NATCHO" STEPHENS:
So when we got in last night,

00:02:11.464 --> 00:02:14.167
it was all we could do to just
get shelter up, basically,

00:02:14.234 --> 00:02:15.969
and get the things
that we needed

00:02:16.035 --> 00:02:19.439
to get a decent night's sleep.

00:02:19.506 --> 00:02:22.175
We've got a home
that's relatively

00:02:22.242 --> 00:02:26.379
comfortable, relatively warm.

00:02:26.446 --> 00:02:30.083
Now, it's time to organize
and settle in so that we

00:02:30.149 --> 00:02:32.852
can be ready for filming.

00:02:32.919 --> 00:02:34.320
ROB POLLARD: Anyone
that works on this show,

00:02:34.387 --> 00:02:35.555
you can't be complacent.

00:02:35.622 --> 00:02:37.790
You need to prepare
properly every time you go

00:02:37.857 --> 00:02:39.425
in something bad could happen.

00:02:39.492 --> 00:02:42.195
You don't want to be out
there in a sticky situation.

00:02:44.931 --> 00:02:48.601
Here we are, in Dead
Horse, inside the hangar.

00:02:48.668 --> 00:02:50.703
We're going into Kavik.

00:02:50.770 --> 00:02:55.108
Sue hasn't been at Kavik
for quite a bit of time.

00:02:55.174 --> 00:02:58.945
So we're going to go in
planning for the worse,

00:02:59.012 --> 00:03:00.847
hoping for the best
when we get there.

00:03:00.914 --> 00:03:03.182
We have quite a bit of
camera equipment here.

00:03:03.249 --> 00:03:06.085
A show like "Life
Below Zero" requires us

00:03:06.152 --> 00:03:08.555
to travel with a lot of gear.

00:03:08.621 --> 00:03:12.926
This isn't your standard show
where you can drive in a car,

00:03:12.992 --> 00:03:15.094
get to set, and start shooting.

00:03:15.161 --> 00:03:18.364
We're going in not knowing
what we're going to get into.

00:03:18.431 --> 00:03:21.334
So we go as prepared
as possible.

00:03:28.641 --> 00:03:30.009
We don't know what
to expect at camp.

00:03:30.076 --> 00:03:33.580
So we've got full GoPros rigged.

00:03:33.646 --> 00:03:37.750
My focus is always on trying to
capture what we expect to see.

00:03:37.817 --> 00:03:39.452
And that is going to be--
we're going to be flying

00:03:39.519 --> 00:03:40.587
over the camp to check it out.

00:03:40.653 --> 00:03:42.288
So we've got a
camera looking down,

00:03:42.355 --> 00:03:44.157
camera on the wing looking
at her as she's driving.

00:03:44.223 --> 00:03:45.992
And then obviously her as
she's looking out the window.

00:03:46.059 --> 00:03:47.293
We can't get in there.

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:50.096
So it's just going to be GoPros.

00:03:50.163 --> 00:03:52.765
We just enjoy the ride.

00:03:52.832 --> 00:03:54.500
MAN: Our number one
concern is safety--

00:03:54.567 --> 00:03:56.803
everything is safe and
everyone is safe-- so that we

00:03:56.869 --> 00:03:58.438
can continue doing our work.

00:04:03.943 --> 00:04:06.179
BRAD CARPER: Personal
gear is over here, guys.

00:04:06.245 --> 00:04:08.147
So we're going out to
Andy [inaudible] place.

00:04:08.214 --> 00:04:09.315
I'm really excited
to go out there.

00:04:09.382 --> 00:04:11.284
But there's a lot of
logistics involved

00:04:11.351 --> 00:04:12.919
with getting to Andy's.

00:04:12.986 --> 00:04:14.320
We start in Fairbanks.

00:04:14.387 --> 00:04:16.422
We fly to Eagle
on a small plane.

00:04:16.489 --> 00:04:19.859
And then they basically-- we
put all of our stuff here.

00:04:19.926 --> 00:04:21.394
And then we get on an
even smaller plane.

00:04:21.461 --> 00:04:22.762
And then we just
do multiple trips

00:04:22.829 --> 00:04:25.431
for about five or six hours
until everything's out there.

00:04:25.498 --> 00:04:28.201
Then we get on snow
machines, sleds.

00:04:28.267 --> 00:04:30.870
And we basically haul everything
to our cabins and get set up.

00:04:30.937 --> 00:04:32.972
But the main thing here is
that when you're filming people

00:04:33.039 --> 00:04:36.075
living off the grid, we have
to live off the grid too.

00:04:36.142 --> 00:04:37.744
in order to really
capture that story,

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:39.245
we have to live that life.

00:04:39.312 --> 00:04:41.080
So right here, we
basically have all

00:04:41.147 --> 00:04:45.151
of our food items, our camera
gear, fuel here for cooking.

00:04:45.218 --> 00:04:47.854
We're in a very remote place,
so we kind of have to be self

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:49.422
sustainable from the beginning.

00:04:49.489 --> 00:04:50.723
Oh, man, this is a tight space.

00:04:50.790 --> 00:04:51.524
Woo!

00:04:51.591 --> 00:04:54.627
It's tiny.

00:04:54.694 --> 00:04:56.129
Smaller than the outhouse
I'm gonna be using.

00:05:20.119 --> 00:05:21.254
This is where we're going.

00:05:21.320 --> 00:05:23.423
We're gonna land on
this lake down here.

00:05:23.489 --> 00:05:25.158
It's a very windy area.

00:05:25.224 --> 00:05:26.392
There's a lot of
mountain terrain.

00:05:26.459 --> 00:05:27.427
There's low trees.

00:05:27.493 --> 00:05:29.395
And then he
basically has to make

00:05:29.462 --> 00:05:30.997
a perfect landing on this lake.

00:05:31.064 --> 00:05:32.265
And it's just
complete glare ice.

00:05:35.968 --> 00:05:37.837
So it was a really
bumpy landing.

00:05:37.904 --> 00:05:39.272
But we're here.

00:05:39.338 --> 00:05:42.041
Then the real work begins.

00:05:42.108 --> 00:05:43.409
The way we get the true story.

00:05:43.476 --> 00:05:44.744
We're not living in a hotel.

00:05:44.811 --> 00:05:46.979
I mean, we are literally
in a remote place.

00:05:47.046 --> 00:05:48.981
And in order to capture
that true story,

00:05:49.048 --> 00:05:51.684
we have to live
that lifestyle too.

00:05:51.751 --> 00:05:54.654
It's time to go live off
the grid for a little bit.

